# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OfficePilot — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` (local dev) or `.env.production` (VPS) and fill in
# real values. Never commit real secrets.
#
# Generate strong secrets with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32   # for NEXTAUTH_SECRET
#   openssl rand -hex 32      # for ENCRYPTION_KEY, CRON_SECRET, WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET
#
# Source of truth: SPEC.md §15 (Environment Variables) and §17 (Deployment).
# Every var below is read by code in src/, prisma/, worker/, or tests/ —
# audited per task 102.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required: Database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL 15+ connection string used by Prisma (datasource db).
# Read by: prisma/schema.prisma (env("DATABASE_URL")).
# Example: postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/dbname?schema=public
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/officepilot?schema=public

# ── Optional: Integration test database ──────────────────────────────────────
# Separate Postgres database used by `npm run test:int`. Required in CI; in
# local dev the test runner derives it from DATABASE_URL by appending `_test`
# to the database name when this var is unset. The DB name MUST end in
# `_test` so the integration suite's safety guard accepts it.
# Read by: tests/integration/test-database-url.ts.
# DATABASE_URL_TEST=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/officepilot_test?schema=public

# ── Required: NextAuth (Auth.js v5) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Secret for signing JWTs/cookies. MUST be 32+ chars of entropy.
# Read by: src/lib/auth.ts, src/lib/auth-edge.ts.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_32

# Canonical URL of the deployed app. http://localhost:3000 in dev,
# https://office.chitly.live in production. Used to build absolute links in
# follow-up reminder emails.
# Read by: src/app/api/cron/followup-reminders/route.ts.
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Required: Encryption (AES-256-GCM in src/lib/crypto.ts) ──────────────────
# 32 bytes of key material expressed as 64 hex chars. Used to encrypt API keys
# stored in the Setting table (Anthropic key, webhook secret, etc.).
# Read by: src/lib/crypto.ts.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ── Required: Initial admin seed (prisma/seed.ts) ────────────────────────────
# Used once on `npx prisma db seed` to create the single admin user.
# After first login the admin can rotate the password from Settings.
# Read by: prisma/seed.ts.
ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL=admin@chitly.live
ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD=change_me_on_first_login

# ── Required: Anthropic (Claude) API ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by src/lib/claude.ts for AI Analysis insights. The runtime resolver
# prefers this env var and falls back to the encrypted value in
# Setting('anthropic_api_key'). Get a key from https://console.anthropic.com/.
# Read by: src/lib/claude.ts.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Required: Inbound leads webhook (HMAC) ───────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret used to sign POST /api/webhooks/leads requests
# (HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body). The webhook route reads this env var
# directly; missing/empty triggers a hard 500 to fail loudly in monitoring.
# Read by: src/app/api/webhooks/leads/route.ts.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
WEBHOOK_HMAC_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ── Required: Cron auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer token required by /api/cron/* endpoints (daily-digest,
# followup-reminders). Configure your cron worker / system crontab to send
# `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET`.
# Read by: worker/index.ts, src/app/api/cron/daily-digest/route.ts,
#          src/app/api/cron/followup-reminders/route.ts.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ── Optional: Cron worker (worker/index.ts under PM2) ────────────────────────
# Base URL the standalone cron worker (SPEC §17.3) hits when calling the
# /api/cron/* endpoints. Defaults to http://localhost:3000 because PM2
# colocates web + worker on the same VPS.
# Read by: worker/index.ts.
CRON_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# IANA timezone the cron worker uses to anchor its schedules. Defaults to
# Asia/Kolkata so a `'0 9 * * *'` expression fires at 09:00 IST per
# SPEC §10.6, regardless of the host TZ.
# Read by: src/lib/cron.ts (getCronTimezone).
CRON_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata

# ── Required: SMTP (notifications, optional digest delivery) ─────────────────
# Used by nodemailer for follow-up reminders and (future) admin alerts.
# All five vars are required at send time; the mailer throws a descriptive
# error if any is missing or empty. Leave SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASS blank in dev
# to disable outbound mail entirely (the cron route logs + skips).
# Read by: src/lib/mailer.ts.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM="OfficePilot <noreply@chitly.live>"

# ── Optional: Runtime conventions ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node.js / OS-level timezone. Not read by application code, but Node and
# Postgres clients honour it for date formatting. Asia/Kolkata aligns the
# host clock with daily-digest scheduling per SPEC §17.3.
TZ=Asia/Kolkata
